	abstract = {In order to address the problem of high penetration of new energy into the grid, which brings huge intermittency and volatility to the distribution network, and to overcome the shortcomings of the traditional methods such as genetic algorithm and whale algorithm, which are limited and unable In order to construct the most suitable scenarios, this paper considers a distribution network system containing a significant quantity of distributed photovoltaic energy under a high penetration rate. It then builds a stochastic planning model for self-healing of the distribution network by constructing constraint functions and objective functions. The construction of the constraint function and objective function enables the development of a self-healing stochastic planning model for the distribution network. This model is solved using the scenario tree stochastic method and the improved PSO algorithm. Finally, the feasibility of the self-healing optimization method proposed in this paper is verified by applying it to four typical scenarios to demonstrate the limitations of the traditional method. In brief, the methodologies presented in this paper offer superior alternatives to traditional methods. The optimization solution is more expedient and precise, with a discernible positive impact on the self-repair capability of the distribution network and secure operation. © 2024 IEEE.},
