	title = {Bi-objective optimization of a large-scale co-firing biomass supply chain},
	year = {2021},
	journal = {IISE Annual Conference and Expo 2021},
	pages = {1177 - 1182},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85120947259&partnerID=40&md5=a863bc34656fb381972991846883c7d6},
	affiliations = {The University of Texas at San Antonio, San Antonio, TX, United States},
	abstract = {A sustainable alternative to fossil fuels in the energy production sector is biomass, as it may be used in biofuel production and coal-biomass co-firing. Cost-efficient procurement is necessary to compete with nonrenewable energy. Research into the optimization of integrated biomass supply chain (BSC) models contribute to this goal. Hub-and-Spoke networks have been proposed in literature as a modeling approach to design large-scale BSCs to minimize investment, however, environmental aspects should be taking into account in the decision making as greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions are generated from their management due to farming and transportation. To reduce GHGs as well as investment in BSC for co-firing, we propose a bi-objective stochastic Hub-and-Spoke optimization model. Since Hub-and-Spoke networks are NP-hard. The proposed BSC is solved by using a tailored-made solution procedure based on a ε-constraint method in combination with a metaheuristic to provide Pareto frontier approximations with a lower computational burden than state-of-the-art exact methods, such as Bender's Decomposition. The proposed metaheuristic is the Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO) that finds the binary first-stage variables, that is, potential depot allocation. Extensive numerical experimentation is conducted to identify the most promising solution procedures by using a case study in the U.S. North East Region. Preliminary solutions of the trade-off between investment and operations costs against GHG emission reduction may be seen in the Pareto Frontier solution, showing a 17% higher cost when aiming to reduce GHG emission produced in the BSC operations. © 2021 IISE Annual Conference and Expo 2021. All rights reserved.},
	author_keywords = {Bi-objective; Biomass; Metaheuristic; Stochastic programming; Supply chain network design},
	keywords = {Biofuels; Biomass; Decision making; Economic and social effects; Emission control; Fossil fuels; Gas emissions; Greenhouse gases; Investments; Pareto principle; Particle swarm optimization (PSO); Stochastic models; Stochastic systems; Supply chains; Bi objectives; Bi-objective optimization; Biomass supply chain; Co-firing; Greenhouse gas emissions; Hub-and-spoke network; Large-scales; Metaheuristic; Solution procedure; Supply chain network design; Stochastic programming},
